\newlabel{fig:mmdesigns}{{5}{13}{Two designs with the same sample size ($n = 50$) under Equation~\ref {eq:mm} with $V_{\max } = 120$, $K = 8$ and $\sigma = 10$. (a) A narrow nitrogen range gives data that look almost linear and carry little information about the asymptote. (b) A wider range reveals the curvature and the onset of saturation. The solid line is the generating model in both panels.\relax }{figure.caption.10}{}}
